<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulaanbaatar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Niislel Khüree, Urga, Ulan Bator, Ikh Khüree</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulaanbaatar is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuul-river">Tuul River</a>. It began in 1639 as a movable monastery for the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebtsundamba-khutughtu">Jebtsundamba Khutughtu</a> and settled at its present site in 1778; Europeans called it Urga. As Niislel Khüree it was the capital of the Bogd Khanate from 1911, and it was renamed Ulaanbaatar, 'red hero', in 1924 when the Mongolian People's Republic was proclaimed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulaanbaatar.jpg" alt="Ulaanbaatar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zazaa Mongolia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UB_downtown.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
